 "title": "Nitrogen Source Influence on Protein Content and Gene Expression in Various Organisms",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the influence of nitrogen sources on protein content and gene expression in various organisms. P. albidus has a protein content of 23.8% and is influenced by several chemicals, including isoleucine, valine, leucine, and phenylalanine. AAT10.2, a gene or protein, is involved in the transport of BCAA, leucine, and valine, and its mRNA levels are studied in SDM79. T. brucei, an organism, is auxotrophic for BCAA, and BY4742 consumes oxygen. The Gene Expression Omnibus has studied BY4742, and PBS has been treated with BY4742 and grown in PCF T. brucei.",
